```"},{"type":"question","id":"ref-predict","prompt":"What prints — and why? Neither `const` nor the new variable name protects `x` here; decide what the code actually does.","kind":"choice","choices":[{"id":"three","label":"3 — y is its own list, so pushing to it leaves x alone"},{"id":"four","label":"4 — x and y point at one list, and push grew that single list"},{"id":"const-error","label":"Error — x is const, so it can't be modified"}],"allowText":true,"hint":"Two questions in one: does `y = x` copy the list or the reference? And does `const` prevent changes to the list's contents?"}],"createdAt":"2026-09-07T13:40:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:40:00.000Z"}
